"Arial",sans-serif'>            &lt;/span>&lt;span style='font-size:12.0pt'>We may
question whether Judas should be counted among the men called apostles in the
primary sense. Although he originally had that role, he left it (cp. Acts &lt;b>1&lt;/b>:15-22)..
In addition, he did not see the resurrected Christ receive the commission and
enablements distinctive to apostles in the primary sense. With Judas omitted, that
leaves thirteen apostles with Matthias replacing Judas and Paul joining the
class later.&lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>THE NEW TESTAMENT BASIS FOR THE NON-DENOMINATIONAL CHURCH: THE HISTORICAL ARGUMENT</title><link>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/church-ecclesiology/ma-thesis/the-new-testament-basis-for-the-non-denominational-church-the-historical-argument/</link><pubDate>Mon, 16 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/church-ecclesiology/ma-thesis/the-new-testament-basis-for-the-non-denominational-church-the-historical-argument/</guid><description>&lt;style>
